  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Short strophic light song of Cairo's early recording era, flourishing from the 1910s to the 1930s, built on a recurring refrain with verses in Egyptian colloquial Arabic, often witty or risqué, and accompanied by a small takht. Women stars such as Munira al-Mahdiyya and Na'ima al-Masriyya recorded it extensively on 78 rpm discs for labels including Odeon, Gramophone and Baidaphon.",
